    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Summary",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "strong"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After last-child death foreclosure on a group parent, QA saw missing parent force-bill on the statement, Summary interest showing zero or mismatched Accrued vs Original, and excess still visible after principal netting. A later multi-child same-day case also collided on the parent force-bill reference."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Root Cause",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "strong"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Parent last-child path did not always post a dedicated parent partial-cycle force-bill; parent accrued was not reconciled to billed original; parent reschedule payment kept a separate excess component after overpayment was already netted into principal; parent force-bill reference reused only account id + reporting time, so two child claims on the same day collided."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Fix",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "strong"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Parent force-bill is posted on the death-foreclosure path; Accrued is reconciled to Original for Summary; reschedule excess is zero after principal netting; force-bill reference is unique per child claim. Local Dev Verification re-ran the full acceptance checklist under a fail-closed harness (printed FAIL exits non-zero)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Impact",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "strong"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
